Canonical	Current preferred Seito usage
Inherited	Received terminology predating Seito
Seito Construction	Deliberately coined or newly structured by Seito
Working	Useful current formulation still subject to refinement
Open	Deliberately unresolved
Superseded	Earlier formulation preserved historically but no longer controlling
Rejected	No longer accepted

Canonical does not mean ancient.

Inherited does not automatically mean canonical.

Those two rules prevent a great deal of confusion.

